WEBVTT

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.250
Imagine knowing exactly what you want to say…

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:11.260
and having no way to say it out loud.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.130
After a total laryngectomy, the voice box is gone.

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:20.500
Many people can still shape words with their lips, but there's

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:21.990
no sound behind them.

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.820
The words are still there.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:24.950
The voice isn't.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:33.390
Every year, people lose their voices to surgery, injury, and illness.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:37.830
Some use an electrolarynx, a voice prosthesis, writing, or sign.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:40.190
TACIT doesn't replace any of them.

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:41.650
It's one more option.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.160
So we asked a simple question.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.150
What if the words you can still mouth silently became another

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:49.000
way to speak?

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:49.850
That's TACIT.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:52.600
It lives quietly in the notch of your Mac.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.500
We built TACIT at HackUMass, starting from a research visual

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:06.210
speech model, and one question: can it read silent lips well

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.550
enough to help in a real conversation?

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.130
Start it once.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:14.370
TACIT reads your lips through the camera, never your microphone,

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:18.540
and a visual speech recognition model running on your Mac turns

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.530
silent articulation into text.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.240
No sound at all.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:22.890
Just lips.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.450
And the words come back.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.570
The honest answer is: sometimes.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:35.760
On our own recordings, some sentences came back word for word.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.460
Others didn't come close.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:40.030
That's exactly why review comes first.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:45.420
Recognition isn't perfect, so nothing is spoken until you decide.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:48.130
Here, "doing" came back as "going".

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:48.980
You see it.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:49.830
You fix it.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.000
[TACIT voice] “How are you doing?”

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.620
When the words are right, one tap on Speak sends exactly those

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:06.830
words, in the voice you chose, into your call's microphone.

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:09.110
And Stop is always one tap away.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:12.280
But a conversation is more than sentences.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:13.080
It's timing.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:17.120
Hold my turn keeps your place, so nobody talks over you while

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:17.910
you compose.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.690
[TACIT voice] “One moment, I'm responding.”

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:25.360
Saved phrases let you react in a second, in words that sound like you.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:29.260
And for practised phrases, an optional real-time mode speaks

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:32.780
without review, only after you accept a clear warning.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:38.050
My Voice lets you choose how you sound, and preview it privately first.

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:42.570
Help Me Respond turns context you paste in into wording you can edit.

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:46.430
It never listens to your meeting, and it never rewrites the

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:47.940
words TACIT recognized.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:51.270
TACIT is built to fail safely.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.500
Pause drops anything stale.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:57.620
If the recognizer crashes, it restarts on its own.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:59.850
Nothing old is ever spoken.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:04.700
Under the hood: the camera, on-device lip tracking, visual

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:08.930
speech recognition, your review, voice synthesis, and a virtual

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:11.620
microphone that any calling app can use.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:13.190
We're early.

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:16.880
Accuracy varies, and TACIT hasn't been tested with people who've

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:17.870
lost their voice.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:21.440
But we think everyone deserves more ways to be heard, on their

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:22.020
own terms.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:27.050
Communication is autonomy: choosing your words, your timing, and

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:28.060
how you sound.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.880
That's what TACIT is for.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:31.910
TACIT.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:32.850
Your words.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:33.790
Your voice.

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:34.980
Beyond speech.
